<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  doctrine: scripted-release-pipeline

  com.carr.release-pipeline: release what merged to main, by script.

  Decisions 17ef11fa and b729859d (2026-09-24): release is script-triggered.
  Every 15 minutes this ticks ops/release-pipeline.py, which compares each
  lane's origin/main with the last SHA it released (out/release-pipeline/
  state.json) and, when the batch touches release paths, runs the same
  sanctioned command sequence the manual Worker release ran on 2026-09-23 and
  2026-09-24, from a detached worktree at the exact SHA, with stdin closed.
  The DoctorCRE app lane runs npm run release:production the same way.

  A LAUNCH AGENT, NOT A MODEL SESSION (PROP-010's ruling; see
  com.carr.calendar-eventkit.plist). Production credentials are read by the
  release scripts from the files they already read; no session ever holds
  them. A failure stops the lane, records the step and its log, and enqueues
  a repo-write Model Room diagnosis session that can only fix forward by PR.

  RISK: RED — it deploys production. Stop it without a commit by creating
  ~/.config/carr/release-pipeline.off, or set "enabled": false in
  ops/config/release-pipeline.v1.json. A second tick while one is running is
  a no-op (flock).

  INSTALLING IT IS A DELIBERATE HUMAN ACT, and there is no installer script on
  purpose: a bin/install-*.sh is an external-admin ingress that would need a
  SCAC registry successor, and turning on autonomous production release should
  be a conscious step anyway. From the canonical checkout, after reading the
  dry run (ops/release-pipeline.py with its dry-run flag):
    sed "s|{{REPO}}|$PWD|g" ops/launchd/com.carr.release-pipeline.plist \
      > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.carr.release-pipeline.plist
    plutil -lint ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.carr.release-pipeline.plist
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.carr.release-pipeline.plist
  Once installed, ops/config-as-code.py check holds the installed body to this
  file like every other CARR LaunchAgent.

  RunAtLoad is false on purpose: installing the job must never itself start
  a production release.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.carr.release-pipeline</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>{{REPO}}/bin/run-scheduled.sh</string>
    <string>--heartbeat-interval</string>
    <string>3600</string>
    <string>release-pipeline</string>
    <string>launchd.run</string>
    <string>{{REPO}}/.venv/bin/python</string>
    <string>{{REPO}}/ops/release-pipeline.py</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>{{REPO}}</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin:/usr/local/opt/node@22/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/opt/homebrew/sbin:/opt/homebrew/opt/libpq/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>

  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>900</integer>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>{{REPO}}/out/release-pipeline.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>{{REPO}}/out/release-pipeline.log</string>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
